2 CONT Enligt '''The Pennsylvania Magazine of History and Biography''', October 1889: He [Baron Isaac Baner] came to Pennsylvania about 1695. His death occurred on the 11th of November, 1718, and his burial was performed in the Presbyter
2 CONC ian graveyard at Wilmington. He left a widow and four children. - - - Means of travel where therefore sent to them, and they were bought to Sweden in the year 1727"
2 CONT
2 CONT Enligt detta hade han '''fyra''' barn och de sändes "hem" 1727. Enligt annan källa dog det äldsta barnet redan 1708 och således kom tre till Sverige.
