2 DATE ABT 1680
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Denmark
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1764
1 OCCU Kapitonas - Komandoras, mulig er han den danske Officer Kruse, der blev halshugget i St. Petersborg for Fornærmelse mod Menzikoff
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sergent, 1716 Fænrik ved Aalborg nation. Inf.-Reg., 1717 Sekondløjtnant, 1718 Premierløjtnant, afsk. 1720 for at gaa i russisk Tjeneste, hvor han blev antagen som Løjtnant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Jørgen K., synes ikke at have drevet det videre i russisk Tjeneste end til Løjtnant; mulig er han den danske Officer Kruse, der blev halshugget i St. Petersborg for Fornærmelse mod Menzikoff (N. H. T. 2. IV. 455). [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Alexander]: I believe the above to be wrong
2 CONT
2 CONT http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I43180&tree=2
2 CONT *  There seems to be an assumption about his beheading (above), but Erik Amburger's file suggests a rather illustrious military career:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://dokumente.ios-regensburg.de/amburger/index.php?id=84515
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Amburger's detail picks him up as the Unter Leutenant in 1723 and details his further military career. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Further, the information given in this book (about Foreigners at the service in the Russian army) http://nekropolvmf.ru/inostransi.php details Johan Jorgen's father to have an estate in Skorgaard and Ostergaard, which is consisten
2 CONC t with Otto's Estate. 
2 CONT
