1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.nuorisokeskusanjala.fi/fi/Lapsi-%20ja%20nuorisoryhm%C3%A4t/Ymp%C3%A4rist%C3%B6koulu%20Regina/Historiallinen%20oppimismilj%C3%B6%C3%B6%20-%20Regina-koulu/
2 CONT
2 CONT [Kenneth, third Lord Duffus ] He died before 18 March 1733-34,[2] having married (contract dated 30 March 1708) Charlotta Christina, daughter of Eric Sjöblad, governor of Gottenberg, who survived until 1771.[3] He had issue:-
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Eric, who succeeded.
2 CONT *2. '''Charlotta, named in 1778 as one of her mother's executors.'''
2 CONT *3. Anna, married to Baron and Count Marshal Gustaf Adolph Palbitzki of Sweden. She was named in 1778 as one of her mother's executors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] Sutherland Book, i. 334, 348, 351; ii. 55, 56. [2] House of Lords Journals, at date. [3] Edin. Tests., 26 September 1778.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte Regina was  quite a remarkable woman in Finnish history. She was the first person to start free schools for small children (up till then it was the church) and a free library for any one. There is a charitable foundation
2 CONC  still in existence," The Regina foundation". So a very well known early educator of commoners. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately I think no painting of her exists nether of her father Kenneth 3d Lord Duffus (but some things, like a naval clock). 
2 CONT
